# Tic-Tac-Toe

Tic-Tac-Toe built for [The Odin Project](https://www.theodinproject.com/lessons/node-path-javascript-tic-tac-toe) using HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript.

## What It Does

- 3x3 board where clicks place marks, alternate turns, block moves on taken cells, and stop play once someone wins or ties.
- Change names modal (`<dialog>` + `<form>`) so players can pick custom names and symbols.
- Win checks across rows, columns, and diagonals, plus tie detection.
- Restart button to wipe the board and reset the turn back to the first player.
- Different colors for each player's marks and live turn/win status text.

## Built With

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript (IIFEs / module pattern and factory functions)

## Notes from Building It

- Kept the board and game controller inside IIFEs and factory functions instead of scattering variables globally.
- Spent a good chunk of time making sure `activePlayer`, the current symbol, and the turn text stayed in sync when changing symbols or hitting restart—and catching sneaky bugs like empty symbol strings matching `0` on the first click.